hogwarts legacy fans feel very strongly  about romance  relationships and whether or not it  belongs in the game  so here in today's video we're going to  talk about the problems some people have  with romance potentially  being in the game i'll also give you my  personal thoughts on how i think they  can make it work  by the way people of the internet  retrorecontour here and i'm just a dad  who loves games and the stories  they tell and so by being both a husband  and a dad to young children i have a  unique perspective  on relationships and how i think they  could work in the game and if they  should work in the game  now some of you may be asking what  exactly is the issue here  why are some people having a problem  with this well what you have to  understand here is although many of us  grew up as harry potter fans and are  older more mature now the characters we  interact with at hogwarts will range in  age from 11 to 17 and of course i  realize some of you  fall within that age range as well when  it comes to hogwarts though first years  are 11 when they cross the black lake to  step into hogwarts for the first time  and 7th years finishing out their  schooling are 17 of course  and that's where i think some are  uncomfortable with the idea of  romance options considering it's a  school of underage wizards  and hogwarts legacy were expected to  play as a fifth year and if you look  back at the harry potter books as a  reference point that's really the book  where student romance and relationships  started taking on a more prominent role  actually i guess you could say it even  goes back to goblet of fire with braun's  jealousy of hermione and victor crum but  order of the phoenix took it up another  notch with all the relationship drama  between harry and cho  of course in book six there was even  more with ron and lavender's  relationship harry and jenny and so on  i think where people stand on this  really depends on a couple of things  including things like age your own  maturity level and ultimately  what people mean when they say quote  unquote romance  options now i could be totally wrong  here but i would guess that when most  people think  of romance and relationships in video  games they're probably thinking of the  hyper-sexualized examples like  mass effect or the witcher and for me  when it comes to hogwarts legacy that  particular example has just  not been on my radar at all that's not  what i'm thinking when i say  romance or relationships in hogwarts  legacy so those of us who want romance  and hogwarts legacy are definitely not  talking about something like this and i  don't think it would even come close to  something like what you see in the  witcher believe it or not guys i know  hollywood and tb  try to convince us otherwise but stick  with me here  romantic relationships are about way  more than just  purely physical desires i know hard to  believe right  now i made a video previously about all  the features i'd like to see in hogwarts  legacy and i did list  romance as one of those features for me  it all comes down to doing this in a  tasteful  way that's fitting for the kids in this  age group that would be attending  hogwarts at the time  it also needs to be something true to  the world that it's set in  if we were playing as first years  absolutely not it probably wouldn't have  much of a place in the game  but how could this play out in hogwarts  legacy how could relationships enhance  our experience and even enhance the  gameplay in some ways  what are some tasteful examples of  relationship options that would be  appropriate for 5th year students at  hogwarts so let's take a look here at 5  ways avalanche could feature romance in  a way that would be age appropriate and  fitting for an open world action rpg  number one social links if you look to  games like the persona series you'll  notice they also feature kids and  teenagers that go through relationship  struggles  one relationship component of the  persona series is the social link system  for those who aren't familiar this is a  system where the player decides which  friends they'll spend time with each day  but  like the real world you only have so  much time in a day so this means you  can't spend time with  every single friend and these aren't  just limited to romantic relationships  in fact when it comes to hogwarts legacy  we already know we'll be able to choose  companions to aid us in our journey  throughout the game  so it would make a lot of sense if we  had some sort of social system to track  and build relationships with those  companions along the way  number two special storylines when you  reach a certain point in your  relationship with characters throughout  the game perhaps you could unlock  special storylines and missions that are  only available when you've achieved a  close relationship  whether romantic or platonic these could  be segments focused heavily on teamwork  and camaraderie or maybe even some  lighthearted options like a date to  hogsmeade village  hopefully avalanche is able to give  players a wide range of options for our  companions with multiple fully realized  characters so we can choose best friends  and significant others that  jive best with our own personality or  even just the personality we want to  portray in the game  developing these relationships over the  course of an entire game should only  strengthen moments of heightened tension  in the story i mean just look back at  the harry potter series there are so  many  numerous events that were made all the  more impactful because of how much we  cared about the characters and their  relationships  characters like luna neville sirius  lupin of course the trio i mean  so many characters in harry potter that  we felt close to  and felt close to each other through the  relationships they built throughout the  book  number three gameplay enhancements it's  important to remember that as much as we  want a good story this  is a video game after all and gameplay  is ultimately what will make or break  the experience  going back to persona for a bit the  social link system doesn't just affect  the story  there are clear impacts on gameplay as  well from bonus xp to special skills  certain bonds and relationships will  yield different abilities that can be  used in combat  so let's get wild here for a minute and  really think big about this suppose  you're faced with a stealth mission in  hogwarts legacy and you have  one friend who's really good at potions  who could help you brew polyjuice maybe  but then you have this other friend who  kind of lives on the edge and says that  they could help you steal a teacher's  invisibility cloak  both options would aid you in your  stealth mission but would play out  completely differently depending on  which skill you would develop throughout  the game  through your relationship with those  characters and then you have the whole  spell casting component how certain  characters could be better at charms  whereas others are better at  transfiguration  there's really a ton avalanche could do  here and i hope they go  all in on a system like this number four  social events  extracurricular activities such as club  meetings sporting events or school  dances are  key moments for social interaction we  see a number of these throughout the  harry potter series ranging from the  yule ball to quidditch matches and  something  off the wall like nearly headless nick's  death day party attending  these events with either a significant  other or even multiple members of a  close-knit social group would be another  way  avalanche could place relationships at  the forefront of the game  who knows if there will be anything akin  to a yule wall but that one immediately  jumps to mind as an opportunity  to highlight relationships formed  throughout the school year and could  also set up a big story moment  number five custom dialogue we already  know we'll be able to make choices  throughout the game and i think that  should apply to our relationships as  well  by building stronger bonds with our  fellow students at hogwarts we should  unlock special dialogue options that are  only available to close friends or  significant others  this is a small element but one i really  think would help make the world feel  more real and more alive  i mean let's be honest there are certain  people in our own lives who we would  tell certain things and then other  friends where we wouldn't tell them the  same thing  even if we consider them both to be  friends we even see this in the books  when hermione and jenny begin to open up  to one another about their romantic  relationships and we learn about  conversations  after the fact that harry and ron aren't  privy to in the moment this is simply  because hermione doesn't want to open up  with them  on some of those details now i'm curious  if any of you guys out there have tried  out harry potter hogwarts mystery i  remember downloading it when it first  came out played it for a little bit  wasn't really my cup of tea so i moved  on  but it's still a game that they are  pushing out new content for and back  around february they did a special  valentine's day  event again i didn't play it very long  so i don't know how it works but you can  see the trailer playing right now where  they actually had  a specific emphasis on romance so i'm  curious to how they handled it in that  game if any of you know be sure and let  me know down in the comments below maybe  i need to give it another shot try it  out see how things have changed  of course there's also that harry potter  magic awakened game which  i haven't had a chance to try out yet  i'm in the us if any of you have played  that one i don't know if it has a  romance segment or not but that might be  worth looking into as well  i know several of you have been asking  about that one in the comments i really  hope it comes to the us  soon so we can all get a chance to try  it out i haven't played it so i can't  say  exactly how it all works but clearly  between games like this and persona  there is a precedent here for romance  and relationships being  in games that feature underage teenagers  of course i want to hear what you guys  think as well did i sway any of you who  are maybe on the fence about whether or  not this can work or maybe i pushed you  the other way and you don't want this in  the game at all now  either way thank you all so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon
 

